    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.13) stands as our clear anchor, benefiting from an ideal confluence of a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Dobbins. The dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) boosts him into elite territory, making him our primary source of speed\u2014a category we are prioritizing heavily today. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) and **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) provide high-floor power production. Despite facing a stern challenge in Bryan Woo, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start due to his elite 0.465 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** (60.55) earns the UTIL spot as he continues to thrive in the #3 hole, balancing out the tougher matchup against Rogers.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was navigating the bottom of the lineup, where **Nelson Velazquez** (40.76) barely cleared our 40-point threshold to retain a spot. He narrowly outpaced **Dillon Dingler** (37.83), who was held out due to an unfavorable platoon split and a score that fell just below our strict efficiency floor. We are keeping a close watch on the status of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Nelson Velazquez** as their lineups are still pending; should either shift down significantly in the order, we will re-evaluate their utility. We are also wary of the heavy task ahead for **Gary Sanchez** (41.99), whose score is suppressed by an 11% penalty from facing Skubal\u2019s elite arm, but he stays active to capitalize on any rare platoon-favorable mistakes. Overall, we are leaning into our speed threats like **Caleb Durbin** (47.16) to capitalize on the slower deliveries of our opponents' starters to manufacture the SBs necessary to sustain our Roto position.",
